  "source_review_notes": {
    "S2.Thmtheorem2": "Reviewed Main: arbitrary measurable pre-noise oracle and conditional laws, coordinate support bound, initial basin, exact power steps; retains almost-sure bounds at preceding-step scale and bounded-orbit/nonminimum event.",
    "S2.Thmtheorem5": "Reviewed Counterexample UniversalGoodTilt: probability spaces, Borel Clarke selections, deterministic starts, radii, all positive power-comparable schedules, measurable iid uniform noises are inside the good-tilt predicate. The conull set is quantified outside all algorithmic choices.",
    "S3.Thmtheorem1": "Reviewed SourceResults literal bundle: same F, all function classes, exact tilt lower bound and strict 0.99 bound, coercivity and core equality below l1 radius 4.",
    "S3.Thmtheorem2": "Reviewed SourceResults literal bundle: both actual limiting subdifferentials, both actual Clarke subdifferentials, and rectangle inclusion; source objects are not replaced by arbitrary sets.",
    "S3.Thmtheorem3": "Reviewed SourceResults literal bundle: Clarke criticality, non-limiting criticality, nonminimum, actual epigraph nonregularity, and every nonnegative local weak-convexity modulus.",
    "S4.Thmtheorem1": "Reviewed deterministic source bundle with every actual Clarke oracle at every basin point and every bounded perturbation. Its pointwise conclusion is stronger than the source almost-sure statement.",
    "S5.Thmtheorem1": "Reviewed exact scalar absolute-value sign-step estimate with all source hypotheses.",
    "S5.Thmtheorem2": "Reviewed actual signed core recurrence, singular arrangement exclusion, bounded coordinate errors, exact initial/scaled bounds, convergence and consecutive-V exclusion. Dropping nonincreasing steps strengthens the theorem.",
    "A1.Thmtheorem1": "Reviewed all strict A.1\u2013A.3 inequalities, literal gAB and verified Frechet derivative, pathwise gradient recursion, rectangular bounds, convergence and V-to-H conclusion.",
    "A1.SS1.p3": "Reviewed open neighborhood in Fin7 real coordinates; every nearby tuple admits the exact certified trap parameters. No probabilistic assumptions enter the deterministic invariant.",
    "S2.Thmtheorem3": "Reviewed actual DDJ map and original state-through-k/noise-before-k sigma fields. E1 is the measurable ddjG map with actual Borel Clarke selection, E2 is ddj_step_bounds, E3 is ddj_noise_assumption_E3 with conditional mean zero and strict fourth-moment bound, E4 and Algorithm 4.5 are ddj_algorithm_and_E4, and Uniform-noise F is the literal iid Euclidean-disk input. This is the example's own proved data, not an assumed external convergence interface.",
    "S2.Thmtheorem4": "All admissible pre-noise oracles are covered by all_oracles_ordinaryGradient_ae. The random uniform basin initialization is covered by both abstract and canonical joint-initialization recursion statements."
